// Large decision tables.
//
// Tables with eight or more rules build an equality index per input column: cells that are
// literal string, number or boolean equalities (`'a'`, `5`, `true`, `'a', 'b'`, `in [1, 2]`,
// `[5..5]`, `$ == 'a'`) are looked up by value, every other cell (ranges, expressions,
// wildcards) is evaluated row by row. The index is an optimisation only: a large table must
// produce exactly what evaluating its rules top to bottom produces, in both hit policies, for
// every input type, with indexed and non-indexed rules interleaved, across many columns.

// --- Equality index at scale ---------------------------------------------------------------
// One indexed column with 100-200 literal rules: every row is reachable, misses fall through.

